  {
    "id": "c3f3d1efe0e4b8c89c8185cf40ca087a583352a5",
    "individual_note": true,
    "resolvable": false,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3975416495,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Resolved in MR !29 (phase 6 of `docs/ongoing-projects/object-save-fixes-and-arm-pricing.md`).\n\n**Audit of feat 1320 and 1321 grants**, read-only, on 2026-10-08. Production has run the arm\ncount since the 2026-10-04 release (`d5cd6a735`), so the pre-deploy check became an audit of\nlive data:\n\n| Where | Extra Arms (1320) | Four Arms (1321) |\n| -- | -- | -- |\n| World objects: `APPLY_FEAT` affects (33 in all, development and production alike, by the recipe in the plan) | none | none |\n| World mobiles: `Feat:` and `MFeat:` lines (1659) | none | none |\n| Production player files (7428), their `Feat:` sections | none | one, a level 30 Thri-Kreen: the race's own innate |\n| Production `player_save_objs` (509487 rows), `pet_save_objs` (1), `player_save_objs_sheathed` (0), `object_database_bonuses` | none | none |\n| Production `house_data` (7951 rows, 44 houses), the table `House_load()` reads | none | none |\n| Production `lib/house` and `lib/plrobjs` files, which the game opens only to see that a record exists | none | none |\n| The same on the development copy (7097 player files, 489375 rows, 9743 house rows) | none | none |\n\nNo grant changed meaning: nothing carries Extra Arms, and Four Arms gave the same four arms\nbefore the count as after it.\n\n**Decisions**, written into `docs/guides/PLAYER_RACES_REFERENCE.md`:\n\n- An arm is priced by what it opens, not by the rank: the third arm 9 RP (lower sleeves, lower\n  gloves, a third wrist, and a weapon hand that mirrors the first pair's whole primary chain),\n  the fourth 6 RP (a fourth wrist and the hand that makes the pair dual, its trained swings\n  behind feats), each arm past four 1 RP. The two add up to Four Arms' 15 RP: the worn positions\n  split three to one and the weapon hands' swings five candidates to four, so 11 RP of weapon\n  hands split 6 to 5.\n- Mixed sources: a race is priced by the arm count it ends with, whatever mix of Four Arms,\n  Extra Arms and `arm_adjust` produces it. A negative `arm_adjust` is a drawback by the\n  lost-slot row.\n- The single-trait cap exemption stays Thri-Kreen's Four Arms alone; another race taking arms\n  (over the cap in every tier but Epic quest) records its own exemption in composition rule 2.\n- The monk's empty third hand is the swing a weapon there makes (`plan_second_pair()` plans one\n  third-hand chain, set by either, and no candidate of its own): class interaction, not priced,\n  inside the 15 RP. Thri-Kreen stays at 20.0 RP.\n\nCorrected 2026-10-08 after the review of MR !29: the house audit now reads `house_data`, the\ntable the game loads a house from (the `.house` file is only its existence check), and the\nworld-file recipe in the plan takes two-field and CR-terminated `A` records. The result is\nunchanged.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
        },
        "created_at": "2026-10-08T06:58:44.084Z",
